## Fix 1 — executor owner lifetime (`framework/src/runtime/host/app.cpp:2645, 2722, 2750`; `runtime/dispatch/coroutine_executor.cpp:147-151`)
Acquire the shared coroutine-executor owner inside `app_t::run()` execution and pair it with the existing normal/error releases; a configured-but-never-run app holds no owner. No Fanout-specific wait/counter/extra executor. Regression: turn `repro_executor_owner.cpp` into a framework-unit test through the public app/scheduler interfaces (configure+destroy one app, run+stop another, assert no continuation scheduler remains after the last run); keep the Fanout created/released equality assertion.

## Fix 2 — durable-operation termination on admitted-peer removal (`runtime/mesh/raw_mesh_node_owner.cpp:996-1004` owner predicate; `:3880-3887` monitor disconnect; `:3975-3980` liveness expiry)
After the admitted peer is removed by either path, evaluate the existing termination predicate (no discovery expectation ∧ no admitted peer → `route_unavailable` for that target's pending durable operations). One predicate, evaluated whenever either input fact changes; no new state/timer/retry, no error-kind remapping in the sample. Regression: turn `repro_join_owner_loss.cpp` into framework-unit tests for both orders (expectation removed then peer lost via monitor disconnect; via liveness tick with an advanced clock argument) asserting the ActorJoin completes `Unavailable`; keep the existing tests that physical loss with a retained expectation stays pending until the admission-dependent deadline.

